{
 "section_summary": "Pages 80–88 conclude a January 1941 issue of Radio Tokyo with broadcast schedules, cultural articles, language lessons, economic commentary, and listeners’ letters. Three State Department cover notes forward that issue to other agencies, followed by a Tokyo consular despatch transmitting March and February editions of Overseas Broadcast. Pages 93–104 begin the February Europe and Near East edition, with schedules and articles on Japanese culture, landscape, student life, art, and history.",
